          "answer": "Based on my examination of the project structure, here's what each file under src/ is for:\n\n**src/api/**\n- `auth.py`: Handles token authentication for all API routes\n- `routes.py`: Defines the HTTP routes and their handlers\n\n**src/core/**\n- `config.py`: Contains runtime configuration settings (reorder threshold, cache TTL, etc.)\n- `db.py`: Database connection and query handling\n- `cache.py`: Cache management functionality\n\n**src/inventory/**\n- `items.py`: Manages item records and catalogue information\n- `stock.py`: Handles stock levels and inventory tracking\n- `reorder.py`: Implements reorder policies for inventory replenishment\n\n**src/shipping/**\n- `carriers.py`: Manages carrier selection for shipping\n- `labels.py`: Handles label creation and booking for shipments\n\n**src/util/**\n- `text.py`: Text processing utilities\n- `time.py`: Time-related utilities\n\nThe architecture is organized with clear separation of concerns:\n- The API package handles HTTP requests and authentication\n- The core package provides foundational services (config, DB, cache)\n- The inventory package manages what's in stock\n- The shipping package handles outbound shipments\n- All packages follow a one-way dependency structure to maintain clean architecture",
